d 'STATPLOT': module for plots of summary statistics, including by category 
d
d   statplot plots summary statistics. It is a wrapper for graph
d hbar, or bar, or dot. It is offered as an alternative command
d that may on occasion produce graphs that are more congenial or
d more convenient than those yielded by the equivalent Stata
d commands. The graphs produced are typically based more on axis
d labeling than on the use of legends, and typically are shown in
d one color rather than several. Version 1.3.0 added confidence
d intervals (ci, level(), ciopts()), percentages and shares
d (percent, share, base()), label wrapping (wrap()), control of the
d order in which variables are plotted (sort, descending, order(),
d first(), last()), heading and group brackets on the category axis
d (headings(), groups()), and export of the collapsed results set
d that is graphed (savedata(), listdata, frame()); statplot is
d rclass and returns its results in r(). Version 1.3.3 draws
d category labels of any length in full on every Stata version;
d wraps labels written in scripts that do not use spaces between
d words, such as Chinese, Japanese and Thai, measuring width in
d display columns; orders groups under ci as graph hbar does; and
d keeps each grouping variable's own values and value labels in
d exported results. Every option added since 1.2.7 is optional and
d with none of them the behaviour is unchanged. A test battery
d ships with the package as an ancillary file. 
d
d KW:  graphics
d KW: summary statistics
d KW: bar chart
d KW: dot chart
d
d Requires: Stata version 8.2
d
